Unless you're playing with illiterate or some other conduct that makes 
it impossible to enchant by normal means, good players won't gain 
anything from this YANI; they're already enchanted up. If you are 
playing with those conducts it's not hard at all to extend the conduct 
on to forbid enchanting by R. It's a self imposed restriction anyway.

The way I see it, the change really just makes confused R even more 
dangerous in that by the time you reach the disenchanters you're 
probably wielding a weapon that will vaporize in a single blow. It's 
sort of a wolf in sheep's clothing, looking like it'd help you out when 
in fact it only hurts you.

You can't completely ignore the new feature unless you were already 
genociding R's before you encounter them anyway. You never know when one 
of them will become confused on accident.


